[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]RespawnBlocks – Documentation[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

All files are in [I]plugins/RespawnBlocks/[/I]. After editing a file by hand, use [B]/rb reload[/B].

[LIST]
[*][B]config.yml[/B]: general settings
[*][B]messages.yml[/B]: prefix, chat messages and GUI texts
[*][B]blocks.yml[/B]: respawn blocks (also editable in the GUI)
[*][B]regions.yml[/B]: respawn regions per world (also editable in the GUI)
[*][B]data.yml[/B]: blocks waiting to respawn. [COLOR=#ff0000]Don't edit this file[/COLOR], the plugin manages it.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]config.yml[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SPOILER="config.yml"]
[CODE=YAML]# Master switch. When false, blocks in respawn regions break normally.
enabled: true

# Block that replaces a mined block until it respawns.
# A block in blocks.yml can override this with its own "placeholder".
default-placeholder: BEDROCK

# Default respawn time (seconds) for blocks added without a time.
default-respawn-time: 60

# NATURAL   - normal vanilla drops on the ground (fortune / silk touch work)
# INVENTORY - normal vanilla drops, put straight into the player's inventory
# BLOCK     - the block itself goes into the inventory (classic MineIsland behaviour)
drop-mode: INVENTORY

# Cancel breaking blocks in a respawn region that are NOT respawn blocks.
block-other-breaks: true

# Allow breaking respawn blocks even when another plugin (for example WorldGuard
# with "build deny") cancelled the break.
override-protection: true

# Ignore players in creative mode.
ignore-creative: true

# Respawn checks run every X ticks (20 ticks = 1 second).
check-interval-ticks: 20

# Waiting blocks are saved to data.yml every X minutes (and on shutdown).
autosave-minutes: 1

# On shutdown, instantly respawn every placeholder in a loaded chunk.
respawn-loaded-on-shutdown: true

# Effect when a block respawns. Sound name or key, NONE to disable.
respawn-effect:
  sound: BLOCK_STONE_PLACE
  volume: 0.6
  pitch: 1.0
  particles: true[/CODE]
[/SPOILER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]blocks.yml[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Every block has a respawn time in seconds. [I]placeholder[/I], [I]drop-mode[/I] and [I]enabled[/I] are optional. When you leave them out, the defaults from config.yml are used.
[SPOILER="blocks.yml example"]
[CODE=YAML]blocks:
  COAL_ORE:
    respawn-time: 30
  DIAMOND_ORE:
    respawn-time: 180
  EMERALD_ORE:
    respawn-time: 240
    placeholder: STONE
    drop-mode: BLOCK
  OAK_LOG:
    respawn-time: 30
    enabled: false[/CODE]
[/SPOILER]
Blocks that don't exist on your server version (for example deepslate and copper ores on 1.16) are ignored, but stay in the file. They start working automatically after a server update.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]regions.yml[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SPOILER="regions.yml example"]
[CODE=YAML]regions:
  world:
    mine: true        # enabled
    vip_mine: false   # disabled
  world_nether:
    nether_mine: true[/CODE]
[/SPOILER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]messages.yml[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Every chat message, the prefix and every GUI text can be changed.
[LIST]
[*]Color codes: [I]&a[/I], [I]&l[/I], ... and hex colors as [I]&#RRGGBB[/I].
[*]Placeholders: [I]%region%[/I], [I]%world%[/I], [I]%block%[/I], [I]%time%[/I], [I]%amount%[/I], [I]%placeholder%[/I] and [I]%label%[/I].
[*]Leave a message empty ([I]''[/I]) to not send it at all.
[*]The time format (for example [I]1m 30s[/I]) can be changed under [I]time:[/I].
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]How it works[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]A player breaks a block. RespawnBlocks checks whether it is a respawn block inside an [B]enabled respawn region[/B].
[*]The break happens normally, so drops, Fortune, XP, durability and other plugins all work as usual.
[*]One tick later, the spot is filled with the [B]placeholder[/B].
[*]Every second, blocks whose time is up and whose [B]chunk is loaded[/B] are put back.
[*]Blocks in [B]unloaded chunks[/B] wait, and respawn as soon as their chunk loads. Chunks are never force-loaded.
[*]Waiting blocks are saved to disk, so they survive restarts and crashes.
[/LIST]
Only the placeholder (or air or liquid) is ever replaced. If something else was built on that spot in the meantime, it is left alone.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]FAQ[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[B]Players see "Hey! Sorry, but you can't break that block here." while mining.[/B]
That message comes from WorldGuard when the region has [I]build deny[/I]. The ore is still mined because of [I]override-protection[/I]. To get rid of the message, allow breaking in the region and let RespawnBlocks protect the other blocks:
[CODE]/rg flag mine block-break allow[/CODE]
Keep [I]block-other-breaks: true[/I] in config.yml.

[B]A placeholder doesn't respawn.[/B]
Its chunk is probably not loaded. It respawns as soon as a player comes near. You can also force it with [I]/rb respawnall[/I]. Admins with [I]respawnblocks.bypass[/I] in creative mode can break a placeholder to cancel its respawn.

[B]Can I use something other than bedrock as placeholder?[/B]
Yes. Change [I]default-placeholder[/I] in config.yml, or set one per block in the GUI: open the block and click a block in your inventory.

[B]Does it work with FastAsyncWorldEdit?[/B]
Yes. RespawnBlocks only talks to WorldGuard.

[B]Which WorldGuard version do I need?[/B]
Any WorldGuard 7.x that matches your server version. For example, 7.0.4 – 7.0.6 for 1.16.5, and the latest version for 1.21.

[B]I'm coming from the old MineIsland plugin.[/B]
Add your mine regions again with [I]/rb region add <region>[/I]. [I]/mineisland[/I] still works as an alias. Set [I]drop-mode: BLOCK[/I] to keep the old behaviour where players receive the ore block itself.
